WEBVTT

00:12.602 --> 00:14.604
[opening theme song playing]

00:25.741 --> 00:30.078
FOOL NIGHT

02:02.420 --> 02:04.464
[Jin] What?
A child was involved as well?

02:04.673 --> 02:06.258
[detective]
I don't know if it's a coincidence,

02:06.341 --> 02:08.885
but the same thing happened
in the previous murders.

02:08.969 --> 02:12.681
It also seems like
only rich people are being targeted. Hmm.

02:15.267 --> 02:16.977
Uh…

02:21.148 --> 02:23.358
All of their belongings were taken.

02:23.441 --> 02:25.777
- [Yomiko grunts softly]
- Was anything left behind?

02:28.321 --> 02:29.322
Candy.

02:31.449 --> 02:34.995
These are all Spiriflora
without flesh or bones.

02:35.078 --> 02:36.997
None of these could be the culprit.

02:38.206 --> 02:41.376
I didn't know that some of the victims
you've found were children.

02:41.835 --> 02:43.003
[Jin exhales]

02:43.295 --> 02:44.337
Where's Toshiro?

02:45.255 --> 02:48.466
[Yomiko] I haven't officially asked him
to help out with the investigation.

02:48.550 --> 02:51.094
[Jin] If you only have
a superpower for two years,

02:51.178 --> 02:52.929
why wouldn't you use it?

02:53.013 --> 02:53.972
[Yomiko exhales]

02:54.472 --> 02:57.642
You want him to find that girl
in your locker too, right?

02:57.726 --> 02:59.895
You had no right to look at that!

03:01.438 --> 03:04.190
[reception] The deposit for
Ms. Kaori Kamiya's hospitalization

03:04.274 --> 03:05.567
is 100,000 yen.

03:18.496 --> 03:19.331
[inaudible]

03:26.630 --> 03:27.797
[inaudible]

03:31.176 --> 03:32.469
[Toshiro sighs]

03:36.556 --> 03:39.267
[Toshiro] <i>Why… why has it come to this?</i>

03:40.602 --> 03:42.020
[cell phone buzzing]

03:43.647 --> 03:46.274
YOMIKO

03:47.442 --> 03:48.360
[Toshiro] <i>What's up?</i>

03:48.443 --> 03:50.111
Oh, hey there, uh…

03:50.820 --> 03:52.489
You met with your mother, right?

03:53.490 --> 03:54.783
How was it?

03:54.866 --> 03:56.243
<i>Yeah, I did.</i>

03:56.326 --> 03:57.911
<i>She's being hospitalized.</i>

03:59.496 --> 04:00.580
[Yomiko] I see.

04:01.039 --> 04:02.249
That's why you called?

04:02.874 --> 04:07.462
Actually, I've been assisting the police
in one of their cases…

04:08.046 --> 04:10.757
and I was just wondering
if you could help, too.

04:14.761 --> 04:17.555
Also, there's another thing
I wanted to ask.

04:18.431 --> 04:20.809
This would be a personal one
from me though.

04:22.018 --> 04:24.396
<i>I want you to locate</i>
<i>an old acquaintance of mine.</i>

04:24.479 --> 04:26.856
<i>A mentally unstable woman</i>
<i>who tried to go to Antarctica--</i>

04:26.940 --> 04:27.774
Sorry. No.

04:27.857 --> 04:28.858
Uh…

04:29.276 --> 04:30.527
<i>I don't have the time.</i>

04:31.736 --> 04:35.031
I only have two years
until I become a Spiriflor.

04:35.949 --> 04:38.159
I feel like I should be

04:38.243 --> 04:40.912
<i>thinking about how I want to live</i>
<i>the rest of my life.</i>

04:41.955 --> 04:43.748
Wait, but… Did something happen?

04:44.666 --> 04:45.667
Sorry.

04:45.750 --> 04:48.795
But I'll keep working
for the Locator Division though. Okay?

04:49.254 --> 04:50.463
<i>Bye.</i>

04:50.547 --> 04:52.215
Hey, just wait a minute!

04:53.300 --> 04:56.177
Do you think… Do you think you would
want to do it if I paid you?

05:00.140 --> 05:01.099
<i>I can't.</i>

05:01.975 --> 05:03.935
<i>I'm just scared of running out of time.</i>

05:04.019 --> 05:05.061
[line disconnects]

05:07.063 --> 05:08.315
[sighs heavily]

05:11.860 --> 05:13.445
DOWN WITH THE TRANSFLORATION SYSTEM!

05:19.075 --> 05:20.869
TRANSFLORA MEDICAL

05:20.952 --> 05:23.538
[static buzzing]

05:35.717 --> 05:37.594
[footsteps approaching]

05:40.805 --> 05:41.848
So, I'm curious.

05:41.931 --> 05:44.267
Do you know what I'm
thinking about right now?

05:45.018 --> 05:46.102
That I'm being lazy?

05:46.186 --> 05:47.687
I want you to really listen.

05:47.771 --> 05:50.106
[Spiriflora buzzing]

05:53.234 --> 05:55.862
[Toshiro] Expectations… hostility.

05:55.945 --> 05:57.238
[Jin] Hmm.

05:57.322 --> 05:58.281
[light pop music playing]

05:58.364 --> 06:00.450
I play poker with my friends here.

06:00.533 --> 06:03.495
I keep losing all my money
and I can't figure out why.

06:03.578 --> 06:05.497
I can't even afford dry cleaning now.

06:06.164 --> 06:09.292
I just want you to listen
to the Spiriflora inside from out here.

06:09.375 --> 06:11.211
And let me know if anyone
that I'm playing with

06:11.294 --> 06:13.505
is starting to think they might
win the round, okay?

06:13.588 --> 06:14.881
You want to cheat?

06:14.964 --> 06:16.216
[Jin] It's not cheating.

06:16.299 --> 06:18.968
The whole point is to play
with everything you've got!

06:19.052 --> 06:20.095
It's cheating!

06:20.845 --> 06:22.889
If I'm about to win, pull this wire once.

06:22.972 --> 06:25.475
If I'm about to lose,
pull it twice, got it?

06:26.392 --> 06:27.811
I'll give you a cut, too.

06:31.397 --> 06:33.858
Are you content with your life, Chief?

06:35.068 --> 06:36.069
Content?

06:36.152 --> 06:38.238
Why? Do I seem sad and pathetic to you?

06:39.405 --> 06:42.242
Well, I'm realizing I have two years left.

06:43.034 --> 06:47.997
So I just have this feeling that I should
think about what the meaning of life is.

06:49.874 --> 06:52.085
I'm guessing having fun
isn't enough for you?

06:54.212 --> 06:56.881
Do you believe there's a reason
that you were born?

07:00.927 --> 07:02.095
Yeah.

07:02.929 --> 07:04.013
I do.

07:06.099 --> 07:07.517
[pop music continues playing]

07:07.600 --> 07:09.602
[Himejima] It's been a while, Yomiko.

07:10.103 --> 07:12.272
Chief forced me to come here tonight.

07:12.689 --> 07:15.150
[Himejima] Well, that's tough luck, kid.

07:15.400 --> 07:16.693
[Toshiro] <i>Yomiko's here?</i>

07:17.277 --> 07:19.571
Hey, you want a drink, Kurakiri, or what?

07:19.654 --> 07:21.281
[Kurakiri] Uh… what is that?

07:21.364 --> 07:22.991
[Himejima] Whiskey made from convicts

07:23.074 --> 07:25.577
who were turned into malt
through Transfloration.

07:25.660 --> 07:27.495
[Kurakiri clears throat]
I think I'll pass.

07:27.579 --> 07:30.540
You shouldn't be flaunting something
you got on the black-market.

07:30.623 --> 07:33.251
It tastes a bit like the Repital Prison.

07:34.335 --> 07:37.547
By the way, Himejima,
what happened with that murder?

07:37.630 --> 07:39.257
The one that had no evidence.

07:39.799 --> 07:41.676
We think it was the work of someone

07:41.759 --> 07:44.721
who's right in the middle
of the Transfloration process.

07:44.804 --> 07:49.392
If anyone were to find out about that,
the Anti-Transfloration groups would riot.

07:49.476 --> 07:51.352
Still isn't enough to shut us down.

07:51.436 --> 07:54.314
I think Transflora Medical
could deal with it.

07:54.397 --> 07:58.318
However, we'd like to get it cleared up
just to prevent any further issues.

07:59.235 --> 08:00.862
So that's all you were thinking

08:00.945 --> 08:03.323
while you were helping
with the investigation?

08:04.199 --> 08:05.325
Of course it was.

08:05.408 --> 08:06.493
I mean, that's just how it is.

08:07.660 --> 08:09.537
I have to say though, I do have my doubts

08:09.621 --> 08:12.707
that someone so far along
in the Transfloration process,

08:12.790 --> 08:16.127
someone void of humanity,
would murder anyone like that.

08:18.254 --> 08:21.841
By the way, have you asked our friend
with the super powers?

08:22.383 --> 08:23.301
[Yomiko] Huh?

08:23.384 --> 08:24.385
[Jin] Toshiro.

08:25.720 --> 08:26.721
[Yomiko] Yeah, sorry.

08:27.347 --> 08:30.058
He refused to be involved
in the investigation.

08:30.141 --> 08:32.060
[Jin] Even with your personal matter?

08:32.977 --> 08:35.855
Finding that person was
the most important thing to you, right?

08:35.939 --> 08:36.773
[Yomiko] Yeah.

08:36.856 --> 08:39.442
[Kurakiri] Oh. Are you
looking for someone, Yomiko?

08:39.526 --> 08:40.401
You want me to help?

08:40.485 --> 08:42.195
[Yomiko] I don't think
you could, Kurakiri.

08:42.278 --> 08:43.321
[Kurakiri] Oh.

08:43.404 --> 08:46.658
[Toshiro] <i>I… I didn't know</i>
<i>it mattered to her so much.</i>

08:47.700 --> 08:49.244
[pop music continues playing]

08:50.245 --> 08:51.079
I'll raise you.

08:51.162 --> 08:52.914
[Jin grunting]

08:55.625 --> 08:57.544
Huh? [clears throat]

08:57.627 --> 09:00.213
[Jin clears throat]

09:02.382 --> 09:04.300
KAORI & TOSHIRO KAMIYA

09:04.384 --> 09:06.302
ENTRANCE CEREMONY

09:13.268 --> 09:14.894
[scribbling]

09:17.647 --> 09:19.482
[scribbling frantically]

09:23.444 --> 09:26.239
ORAL MEDICATION
KAORI KAMIYA, THREE TIMES A DAY

09:32.537 --> 09:35.665
[Toshiro] <i>Another day ended</i>
<i>without me accomplishing anything.</i>

09:39.919 --> 09:41.004
<i>What is it?</i>

09:42.380 --> 09:45.216
<i>The meaning of… life.</i>

09:45.883 --> 09:46.968
[groans]

09:47.927 --> 09:48.928
[thumping]

09:55.268 --> 09:56.311
[slithering]

10:17.373 --> 10:19.959
NITTEBORO
SEAFOOD-FLAVORED NOODLE SOUP 1

10:22.670 --> 10:24.255
UNUSUAL CASES
OF LATE STAGE TRANSFLORATION

10:37.310 --> 10:41.689
Mom, my homework's all done now.
Can I play a game?

10:41.773 --> 10:43.858
Review your work first.

10:43.941 --> 10:45.193
I did review it.

10:45.276 --> 10:47.612
You said that before,
but you still got some wrong.

10:47.695 --> 10:51.032
Your schoolwork's very simple,
so you should be getting it right.

10:51.115 --> 10:53.785
I send you to cram school
five days a week.

10:54.994 --> 10:57.830
I know I did it perfectly though,
this time.

10:57.914 --> 10:58.748
So can I--

10:58.831 --> 10:59.874
Show me your work.

10:59.957 --> 11:02.377
If anything's wrong I'll throw out
your game console.

11:03.920 --> 11:05.254
I'll review it again.

11:11.427 --> 11:13.346
[scribbling frantically]

11:14.055 --> 11:15.640
[sobbing softly]

11:16.516 --> 11:17.934
[children chattering]

11:21.938 --> 11:23.648
- [young Toshiro] Out of the way.
- [keyboard honking]

11:26.192 --> 11:27.777
Jeez, what's with him?

11:31.155 --> 11:33.241
[male teacher]
Hmm. Your work is perfect, good job.

11:33.324 --> 11:34.742
Learn from her example, everyone.

11:36.160 --> 11:37.412
[boy 1] What a nerd.

11:37.495 --> 11:39.789
- [girl 1] She's such a show-off.
- [girl 2] Teacher's pet.

11:40.456 --> 11:42.375
- [girls snickering]
- [boy 2] Does she have any friends?

11:42.458 --> 11:43.376
She's so awkward.

11:43.459 --> 11:44.836
[students chattering]

11:44.919 --> 11:47.296
[boy 3] I've never talked to her,
she's too weird for me.

11:47.380 --> 11:50.591
- [students continue chattering]
- Okay, let's go over cubic equations now.

11:50.675 --> 11:53.511
[students continue chattering
and snickering]

11:54.971 --> 11:57.432
[young Yomiko] My mom says that these
six years of elementary school

11:57.515 --> 12:00.768
are going to determine how
the rest of our lives turn out.

12:00.852 --> 12:02.353
If you want to get a good job,

12:02.437 --> 12:05.273
you have to graduate
from a national university.

12:05.356 --> 12:07.775
To do that, you have to get
into Keio Junior High,

12:07.859 --> 12:11.320
but if you can't you have to try
and get into either Seiko or To-oh,

12:11.404 --> 12:13.197
which are both also hard schools.

12:13.281 --> 12:14.574
The curriculum at other schools

12:14.657 --> 12:17.243
won't help you pass
the university entrance exam.

12:18.327 --> 12:20.580
It's a given that you should be
able to do schoolwork.

12:20.663 --> 12:23.499
In fact, if you can't get
a perfect score after studying,

12:23.583 --> 12:25.126
you won't have a good future.

12:25.209 --> 12:27.211
You'll die young or be a waste of space.

12:31.716 --> 12:33.968
APOLOGY LETTER

12:34.469 --> 12:35.595
How stupid.

12:36.053 --> 12:37.555
- [rattling]
- Hmm?

12:39.140 --> 12:41.225
[writing]

12:44.687 --> 12:45.688
[chair rattling]

12:46.898 --> 12:48.691
I, YOMIKO HORAI

12:51.068 --> 12:52.445
I'll do homework.

12:52.528 --> 12:53.654
MATH II

12:53.738 --> 12:54.906
Wow!

12:55.865 --> 12:56.782
What is it?

12:56.866 --> 12:57.867
That's awesome.

12:57.950 --> 12:59.660
It's a fifth-grade textbook.

12:59.744 --> 13:03.164
The only textbooks my parents bought me
were the ones for first grade.

13:03.247 --> 13:04.749
The cover is so shiny!

13:04.832 --> 13:06.125
It looks brand new!

13:06.667 --> 13:09.128
[young Yomiko]
Some people can't even afford textbooks?

13:10.213 --> 13:11.339
Let me see it.

13:13.508 --> 13:16.135
Okay, we can trade if you want.

13:17.053 --> 13:17.929
MATH II
TSUTSUMI PUBLISHING

13:18.012 --> 13:19.055
Here.

13:21.349 --> 13:22.642
[stifles laughs]

13:23.559 --> 13:24.852
[laughing softly]

13:25.978 --> 13:28.523
I call him "Mr. Horseman."
What do you think of it?

13:29.190 --> 13:30.233
[pleasant music playing]

13:30.316 --> 13:33.402
JAPANESE

13:41.285 --> 13:43.454
[inaudible]

13:45.373 --> 13:47.458
[music continues]

14:01.472 --> 14:03.975
[young Toshiro] Hey, you wanna draw
all over the blackboard?

14:05.101 --> 14:06.185
Sorry, I can't.

14:06.269 --> 14:07.562
I have to go.

14:07.645 --> 14:09.355
[young Toshiro] What? But why?

14:12.441 --> 14:14.068
It was fun getting to play.

14:14.151 --> 14:15.945
Do you wanna play tomorrow?

14:16.028 --> 14:17.572
I have cram school.

14:17.655 --> 14:18.990
The day after that?

14:19.699 --> 14:20.533
Cram school.

14:21.492 --> 14:22.785
Even the day after that?

14:22.868 --> 14:24.787
[melancholy music playing]

14:26.163 --> 14:27.456
When can we play?

14:28.416 --> 14:30.877
Sorry, I don't think I can do this again.

14:30.960 --> 14:32.169
Wait, what do you mean?

14:33.462 --> 14:37.466
I was told I needed to work hard now
so I'm set for the future.

14:37.550 --> 14:40.261
Are you working hard for your future, too?

14:41.095 --> 14:42.263
Not really, no.

14:42.346 --> 14:43.764
You dummy, you'll die young!

14:44.974 --> 14:47.393
[young Toshiro]
Well, I do think the future is important.

14:48.603 --> 14:49.687
But…

14:50.229 --> 14:53.316
I think that the present
is really important also.

14:56.110 --> 14:58.154
[gentle music playing]

15:06.162 --> 15:08.831
[both laughing]

15:08.915 --> 15:10.458
[young Toshiro] Ooh!

15:10.541 --> 15:11.667
[both laughing]

15:14.962 --> 15:16.631
[young Yomiko] You're still gonna die!

15:20.301 --> 15:21.886
[microwave beeps]

15:21.969 --> 15:23.804
[melancholy music playing]

15:23.888 --> 15:25.681
[pen scribbling]

15:38.110 --> 15:40.112
Let's see, where is it?

15:41.113 --> 15:43.074
TSUTSUMI PUBLISHING

15:45.159 --> 15:46.911
[gentle music playing]

15:46.994 --> 15:48.412
[gasps]

15:54.961 --> 15:58.089
YOMIKO

16:04.595 --> 16:05.680
[door opens]

16:07.348 --> 16:08.182
[door closes]

16:10.101 --> 16:11.644
[melancholy music playing]

16:34.750 --> 16:36.669
CONTACTS
TOSHIRO

16:39.839 --> 16:40.840
[sighs softly]

16:49.348 --> 16:50.391
[Toshiro] Yomiko.

16:52.101 --> 16:53.102
Is something wrong?

16:53.519 --> 16:55.104
No. I was just wondering…

16:56.105 --> 16:57.314
Are you mad at me now?

17:00.067 --> 17:01.235
No, of course not.

17:02.570 --> 17:03.738
What are you doing?

17:07.992 --> 17:10.161
[Yomiko] This is the only survivor
of the serial murders

17:10.244 --> 17:11.746
that have been happening.

17:11.829 --> 17:13.581
I'm helping the police with it.

17:14.290 --> 17:15.875
Whoa, this is…

17:16.542 --> 17:18.669
The number of victims is growing.

17:18.753 --> 17:21.589
I want the person doing it to be caught
once and for all.

17:27.136 --> 17:29.055
I… can listen if you want.

17:29.805 --> 17:31.515
Would you really do that?

17:31.599 --> 17:35.061
Oh, you can't have
a conversation though, right?

17:35.519 --> 17:38.272
Uh, I did it once before actually.

17:38.355 --> 17:39.398
The thing is…

17:40.983 --> 17:42.610
You mind leaving the room?

17:42.693 --> 17:44.111
What for?

17:44.195 --> 17:47.281
Can you make a better connection with it
if you're naked or something?

17:47.364 --> 17:48.824
No, that's not it.

17:49.658 --> 17:51.285
Just be quiet for a bit, then.

17:56.415 --> 17:57.458
[Yomiko gasps]

18:02.129 --> 18:03.547
[Spiriflora buzzing]

18:03.631 --> 18:06.509
I need to ask you about
the person who killed you.

18:06.592 --> 18:08.761
Do you know who it was, or what happened?

18:13.140 --> 18:14.683
[Spiriflora buzzing, screeching]

18:14.767 --> 18:16.727
It sounds really confused.

18:16.811 --> 18:18.062
It's screaming so loud.

18:18.145 --> 18:19.855
Now it's crying, questions.

18:21.315 --> 18:23.818
Try to calm down. Talk slowly.

18:27.530 --> 18:28.572
"I was…

18:29.907 --> 18:32.368
happy with where I was in life for once.

18:34.286 --> 18:35.996
And now it's over.

18:37.581 --> 18:38.666
Why?

18:40.584 --> 18:41.669
What for?"

18:54.140 --> 18:55.641
[Toshiro] Are you gonna tell the family?

18:56.684 --> 18:58.310
[Yomiko] They wouldn't believe me.

19:00.479 --> 19:02.857
[Toshiro] I'm sure that was kinda shocking
for you, huh?

19:05.651 --> 19:06.735
[Yomiko] I'm sorry.

19:09.697 --> 19:12.491
I'm sorry for keeping it a secret
that I'm looking for someone.

19:13.784 --> 19:15.703
I figured that you wouldn't mind
helping me with it

19:15.786 --> 19:17.830
while you were working here.

19:19.999 --> 19:21.000
It's fine.

19:21.083 --> 19:22.334
I'm sorry, as well.

19:22.793 --> 19:26.589
Toshiro, I tried to use you
for my own gain.

19:28.340 --> 19:30.718
It seemed like two years
was a lot of time.

19:32.469 --> 19:33.804
Yeah, I thought it was too.

19:33.888 --> 19:34.889
[gasps]

19:39.268 --> 19:40.269
[chuckles softly]

19:42.813 --> 19:44.315
[both laughing]

19:51.280 --> 19:52.656
[Toshiro] You wanna go get some food?

19:52.740 --> 19:54.950
[Yomiko] Yeah. There's a place
I've been wanting to try.

19:55.034 --> 19:56.493
[Toshiro] Okay, let's go.

20:08.297 --> 20:09.298
[male voice] <i>Die.</i>

20:10.007 --> 20:11.008
[gasps]

20:13.302 --> 20:14.720
[gasping]

20:14.803 --> 20:16.222
Watch out!

20:17.473 --> 20:18.682
[Yomiko gasps]

20:19.642 --> 20:21.060
[groaning, gasping]

20:25.272 --> 20:27.858
[warbled mumbling]

20:29.276 --> 20:31.570
- [male voice 1] <i>I'll kill you.</i>
- [female voice 1] <i>Stop it.</i>

20:31.654 --> 20:33.656
- [male voice 1] <i>I'll kill you.</i>
- [male voice 2] <i>Please, stop.</i>

20:33.739 --> 20:35.449
[female voice 2] <i>Aw, poor girl.</i>

20:35.908 --> 20:37.660
[Toshiro] <i>What the hell is that thing?</i>

20:37.743 --> 20:39.995
<i>Is it… a Spiriflor?</i>

20:40.079 --> 20:41.163
<i>Why is it moving?</i>

20:42.539 --> 20:44.375
[panting]

20:46.627 --> 20:47.920
You need to run.

20:49.755 --> 20:51.882
- [explosion]
- [high-pitched trilling]

20:51.966 --> 20:53.384
[Toshiro panting]

20:58.138 --> 20:59.306
[Toshiro] <i>My ears!</i>

20:59.932 --> 21:01.183
<i>What did she just throw?</i>

21:01.767 --> 21:03.686
<i>I have to find a place</i>
<i>with a lot of people.</i>

21:03.769 --> 21:05.980
Yomiko! Yomiko!

21:06.063 --> 21:08.315
<i>Damn it! Don't die!</i>

21:08.399 --> 21:09.650
[panting]

21:09.733 --> 21:11.026
<i>It's not following us.</i>

21:11.860 --> 21:14.071
<i>No, that thing wanted us dead.</i>

21:14.154 --> 21:16.031
<i>There's no way it's giving up.</i>

21:16.115 --> 21:17.866
<i>It's definitely hiding somewhere.</i>

21:19.451 --> 21:20.536
<i>Where is it?</i>

21:20.619 --> 21:22.121
<i>Where is it hiding?</i>

21:22.913 --> 21:24.540
<i>Listen for that bloodlust!</i>

21:24.623 --> 21:25.791
<i>Please, let me hear it!</i>

21:26.542 --> 21:29.253
<i>If I can't hear now,</i>
<i>then what's the point?</i>

21:29.336 --> 21:30.587
<i>I can do this.</i>

21:30.671 --> 21:31.839
<i>I can hear!</i>

21:31.922 --> 21:33.048
<i>My ears don't matter!</i>

21:33.132 --> 21:34.550
<i>Just listen!</i>

21:34.633 --> 21:35.759
<i>Listen!</i>

21:38.637 --> 21:39.638
[male voice] <i>I'll kill you.</i>

21:42.558 --> 21:44.101
[Toshiro grunting, panting]

21:49.606 --> 21:50.858
[exclaiming]

21:51.650 --> 21:52.693
[grunting]

21:58.282 --> 21:59.283
[Yomiko gasps]

22:01.327 --> 22:02.328
[groans softly]

22:06.081 --> 22:07.207
[gasping softly]

22:13.797 --> 22:14.631
[man] Huh?

22:14.715 --> 22:15.841
- [Toshiro grunts]
- [man] Hey…

22:17.301 --> 22:18.927
[weakly] Call… an ambulance…

22:19.762 --> 22:21.930
[Toshiro groaning, coughing]

22:22.514 --> 22:24.516
[closing theme song playing]
